# Package manager: npm (package-lock.json is committed; Cloudflare installs from it).

# Env: `.env` itself is committed on purpose — it holds only public values (project URL and
# publishable key), see DEPLOY.md A1. Every OTHER variant is where a real secret ends up: Vite
# loads `.env.production` on build, so that name invites pasting the secret key. They stay out.
.env.*
!.env.example

